    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:186`), binding an `OwnerFieldsDto` request body.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Security gate\n1. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Request validation (the `@Valid` pass)\nThese all accumulate into one `BindingResult` and fail as **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n\n2. **Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`OwnerFieldsDto.java`):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (allows trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - `title` enum invalid value \u2192 Jackson deserialization failure\n3. **`OwnerFieldsValidator`** (registered via `@InitBinder`) \u2014 rejects blank first/last/city/telephone; requires an address in either structured (`addressLine1`) or flat (`address`) form.\n4. **`PostcodeValidator`** \u2014 if postcode present, checks it's in the city's regional range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any).\n5. **`DisposableEmailDomainValidator`** \u2014 rejects emails whose domain is mailinator.com / tempmail.com / guerrillamail.com.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Idempotency short-circuit\n6. **Idempotency replay** (`replayIdempotentCreate`) \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was already used and that owner still exists, return it with **200 OK** and skip everything below.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Mapping & normalization (mutations on the entity)\n7. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 explicitly ignores `id, pets, customerCode, householdId, namesakeCount, possibleDuplicate, possibleDuplicateOf, deleted`.\n8. **`AddressResolver.resolve`** \u2014 normalizes address (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE), prefers structured over flat, composes the `address` field.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Business-rule validation + more normalization (interleaved, in this exact order)\n9. **`RegistrationDateValidator.validate`** \u2014 if supplied date is in the future \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n10. **Default registration date** \u2014 if null, set to `LocalDate.now()`.\n11. **`BusinessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay`** \u2014 rolls weekends and fixed 2026 public holidays forward to the next weekday.\n12. **`TelephoneNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 strips separators, forces E.164 (`+61` default, length 8\u201315 + country rules); invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n13. **`EmailNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 blank \u2192 null, else trimmed + lower-cased.\n14. **`DailyRegistrationLimitValidator.validate`** \u2014 if \u2265100 owners already registered on that date \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n15. **`CityCapacityValidator.validate`** \u2014 if \u226550 owners already in that city \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (**409**).\n\n## Phase 6 \u2014 Derived-value assignment\n16. **`households.householdId`** \u2014 set to first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)`.\n17. **`HouseholdDuplicateValidator.validate`** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold` is false and a non-deleted owner already has the same householdId \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (**409**).\n18. **Possible-duplicate flagging** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold` true, set `possibleDuplicate=false`; otherwise `PossibleDuplicateDetector.detect` sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` (earliest non-deleted owner with same last name + postcode but different phone).\n\n## Phase 7 \u2014 Persistence side-effects (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, `@Transactional`)\n19. **Customer code** \u2014 if new/null: `CustomerCodeGenerator.generate` (`<REGION>-<HASH8>` from `SHA-256(telephone+lastName)`), then `CustomerCodeDeduplicator.deDuplicate` appends `-<n>` on collision.\n20. **Namesake count** \u2014 if new/null: `NamesakeCounter.count` counts existing owners with same first+last name.\n21. **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 the actual DB insert. (Entity `@NotEmpty`/`@Email`/`@Pattern` E.164 constraints re-checked here; no unique DB constraints exist.)\n\n## Phase 8 \u2014 Post-persist side-effects\n22. **`OwnerAuditLogger.logCreated`** \u2014 writes an INFO line to the dedicated `\"AUDIT\"` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membership level/number).\n23. **`OwnerIdempotencyStore.record`** \u2014 stores key\u2192owner-id in an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap` (first writer wins; blank keys ignored).\n24. **Response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **No** email/notification sending, event publishing, password encoding, role assignment, cache eviction, or JPA `@PrePersist`/auditing callbacks exist in this path \u2014 all derived/timestamp logic is done manually in the controller/service.\n- There is a **doc-vs-code gap**: `OwnerDto.identityKey` is documented as yielding a 409 on a full identity-key match, but the create path only enforces duplicate detection via last-name+postcode (`HouseholdDuplicateValidator`). The identity key is computed for the response only and never checked for uniqueness during create."
